{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.235, "data": {"request_id": "5a3f51bb94ca", "seq": 35, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:15:45.522Z", "t_ms": 10187, "delta": "Text Chunking and Embedding:** RAPTOR divides the retrieval corpus into short, contiguous text chunks of approximately 100 tokens ("}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.414, "data": {"request_id": "5a3f51bb94ca", "seq": 36, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:15:45.700Z", "t_ms": 10365, "delta": "preserving full sentences) and encodes them using SBERT embeddings to form the leaf nodes of a tree [C14]."}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.578, "data": {"request_id": "5a3f51bb94ca", "seq": 37, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:15:45.866Z", "t_ms": 10530, "delta": "\n* **Semantic Soft Clustering:** To group text based on semantic similarity rather than document adjacency, it reduces embedding dimensions with UMAP and"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.755, "data": {"request_id": "5a3f51bb94ca", "seq": 38, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:15:46.043Z", "t_ms": 10708, "delta": " clusters them using Gaussian Mixture Models (GMMs) [C9, C10, C14]. It"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.999, "data": {"request_id": "5a3f51bb94ca", "seq": 39, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:15:46.271Z", "t_ms": 10936, "delta": " uses soft clustering, allowing individual text segments to belong to multiple clusters [C10].\n* **Recursive Tree Construction:** An"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.11, "data": {"request_id": "5a3f51bb94ca", "seq": 40, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:15:46.398Z", "t_ms": 11063, "delta": " LLM (e.g., GPT-3.5-turbo) summarizes each cluster of text chunks [C5"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.411, "data": {"request_id": "5a3f51bb94ca", "seq": 41, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:15:46.674Z", "t_ms": 11338, "delta": ", C14]. These newly generated summary nodes are then re-embedded, clustered again, and summarized iteratively until further clustering is"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.459, "data": {"request_id": "5a3f51bb94ca", "seq": 42, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:15:46.747Z", "t_ms": 11412, "delta": " no longer feasible, forming a multi-layered tree index [C14]."}}
